    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "I fixed it in `audit.go`, but I could not run the test. Each `go test` call was blocked at the approval prompt.\n\n**Cause:** `Record` read the whole `audit.json`, added one event, then wrote the whole file back. When two processes did this at the same time, the second write replaced the first, and that process's event was lost.\n\n**Fix:**\n- Each process now appends to its own file, named `audit-\u003cpid\u003e-\u003crandom\u003e.jsonl`, with one JSON line per event. Processes never write to the same file, so they cannot overwrite each other.\n- A lock inside the process keeps its events in the order it recorded them.\n- `Events` reads every per-process file, plus the old `audit.json` so that earlier events stay in the report. It skips a last line that has no newline, because that write is still running or a crash cut it short.\n\nI added `audit_test.go`. It starts 8 child processes that each record 200 events at the same time. Then it checks that every event is present and that each process's events are in order. To run it: `go test -count=1 ./...`\n\n**TLDR**\nProcesses overwrote each other's copy of `audit.json`. Now each process appends to its own file, and `Events` merges them.\nThe new test in `audit_test.go` has not run because the command was blocked. Run `go test -count=1 ./...`.",
